{"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftml\/earlystoppingcallbacks"]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Early Stopping & Generalization Control","modules":[{"name":"SwiftML"}],"role":"collectionGroup"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides & Tutorials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/SupervisedClassifiers","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/SupervisedRegressors","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/PreparedRegression","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/PreparedClassification","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/CoreMLInference","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/BoundedInference","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/EnsembleLearning","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/HistogramGradientBoosting","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/ReproducibilityAndPRNG","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/MLOpsExport","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/ReusableCPUPrediction"],"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterative estimators like multi-layer perceptrons ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLPClassifier"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLPRegressor"},{"text":") and gradient boosted decision trees (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GradientBoostedTreesRegressor"},{"type":"text","text":") improve their training loss over successive iterations. However, after sufficient capacity has been fit, additional epochs frequently lead to overfitting on training noise and deteriorating generalization on unseen data."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EarlyStopping"},{"type":"text","text":" provides a decoupled, value-type training callback that monitors validation loss or performance metrics across successive epochs, halting training and optionally restoring optimal model weights."}]},{"text":"Mechanics & State Machine","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Mechanics--State-Machine"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["Epoch Evaluation (Score S_t)","            │","            ▼"," Is (Best - S_t) > minDelta?","   ├── YES ──► Reset wait = 0, update bestScore = S_t, checkpoint weights","   └── NO  ──► Increment wait = wait + 1","                 │","            Is wait >= patience?","              ├── YES ──► shouldStop = true, restore best checkpoint weights","              └── NO  ──► Continue training"],"syntax":null},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Configuration Parameters","anchor":"Configuration-Parameters"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"patience"},{"type":"text","text":": Number of consecutive non-improving evaluations tolerated before triggering an early halt."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"minDelta","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": Minimum absolute improvement required to qualify as progress.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"direction"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".minimize"},{"type":"text","text":" for loss functions (cross-entropy, MSE) or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".maximize"},{"type":"text","text":" for scoring metrics (accuracy, R2, AUC)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restoreBestWeights"},{"type":"text","text":": When "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":", automatically restores the model parameters from the epoch that achieved "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bestScore"},{"type":"text","text":", avoiding overfit tail iterations."}]}]}]},{"text":"Example Usage","type":"heading","anchor":"Example-Usage","level":2},{"syntax":"swift","code":["im